{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Silly Superstitions", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Knock on Wood", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 5, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 17, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "  Describe unusual events through a wider range of B1 language in both work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects  in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects  in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects  in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects  in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects  in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects  in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects  in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects  in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn8le17ob05re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to talk about superstitions.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Gerunds and Infinitives", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "A <span class=\"strong\">gerund</span> is a verb ending with -ing (doing).<br/> An <span class=\"strong\">infinitive</span> is to + verb (to do).<br/><br/> There are rules about which verbs you can use with gerunds and which verbs  you can use with infinitives. Also, the gerund can be used as the  subject of the sentence.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Verbs commonly followed by a gerund:<br/><br/>  Verbs that express <span class=\"strong\">likes</span>/<span class=\"strong\">dislikes</span>:  <span class=\"italic\">like, love, enjoy, hate</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example: <span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">like going</span> to my family parties.</span><br>*<span class=\"italic\">like</span>/<span class=\"italic\">love</span>/<span class=\"italic\">hate</span> can also be followed by an infinitive.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "These are some verbs that are followed by an infinitive: <span class=\"italic\"> hope, seem, decide, start</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example: <span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">started to walk</span> towards my car when the accident happened.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use infinitives after adjectives. Example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">was very upset to see</span> that my car had been hit.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "An activity can be expressed as a gerund and function as the subject of the sentence. Example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Getting together with family</span> is always fun.<br/><span class=\"strong\">Knocking on wood</span> is a good idea.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I wanted to keep my luck going.", "type": "example"}, {"content": " I mentioned not having an accident.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "My family members all recalled being in car accidents.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I laughed and refused to knock on anything wooden.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Be Supposed to", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the structure <span class=\"strong\">be supposed to</span> when you want to talk about expectations, obligations or arrangements.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use <span class=\"strong\">be supposed to</span> to talk about situations in the past, present or future.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The structure is:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Subject + To be + supposed to + verb", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">are not supposed to</span> drive away from an accident. <br/>You <span class =\"strong\">were supposed to</span> leave a note. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "**Pronunciation tip**:<br/>When you say be supposed to, you link the /d/ and /t/ sounds together. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Like this:<br/>Be suppose_to", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You are supposed to stay and wait. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You are supposed to leave a note with a phone number.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to acknowledge", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to say that you accept or do not deny the truth or existence of something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: He had to acknowledge that it could be luck.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le17ob05aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "eventually", "type": "name"}, {"content": "at some later time; in the end", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The conversation had turned to cars and eventually to car accidents.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le17ob05aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to exclaim", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to cry out or speak suddenly or with strong feeling", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: They all exclaimed that I better knock on wood.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le17ob05aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "despite", "type": "name"}, {"content": "in spite of; notwithstanding", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(preposition)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I refused to knock on anything wooden, despite the warnings of my aunt.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le17ob05aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "destroyed", "type": "name"}, {"content": " broken beyond repair", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: My car had been  destroyed by someone who hit it and then drove off.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le17ob05aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to drive off", "type": "name"}, {"content": "if a vehicle or driver drives off, the vehicle starts moving and leaves", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(phrasal verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: After he hit my car, the driver started to drive off.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le17ob05aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "victim", "type": "name"}, {"content": "someone or something that is harmed by an unpleasant event (such as an illness or accident)", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I was a victim of a hit-and-run.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le17ob05aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "hit-and-run", "type": "name"}, {"content": " involving a driver who does not stop after causing an accident", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: My car was really damaged because of the hit-and-run.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le17ob05aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "With a partner, research on the internet five expressions, phrases or idioms for good luck.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Do the same for bad luck.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Pick the best three and be able to explain their meanings clearly.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Change partners.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Teach your new partner your three good and bad luck expressions and he/she teaches you theirs.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Change partners with other class members 2 more times.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Return to your original partner and compare your new vocabulary.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Make a list: good expressions on the left, bad on the right.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I talk about manners, customs and superstitions. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about things I am supposed to do and things that are supposed to happen.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about my attitudes toward an action.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I research vocabulary.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share information clearly.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"questions": [], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can talk about manners, customs and superstitions. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " 