}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"content": "\nInstructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self Assessment.\n", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"content": "Speaking", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}]}], "stimuli_ids": [], "template_override": 1, "type": "DWS", "id": 11}], "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "type": "scholar", "stimuli": [{"type": "welcome", "template_override": 1, "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"type": "audio", "template_override": 1, "title": "", "_data": [], "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"coverimg": "engenn8le17ob05re2img05.jpg", "audiosrc": "engenn8le17ob05re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "engenn8le17ob05re2img05.jpg", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"time": "100", "image": "engenn8le17ob05re2img05.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "Tim from Toronto wants to know, \"why are we supposed to knock on wood after we say something good happened to us?\"\n<br/><br/>\nAcknowledging luck and wanting to keep it going is the easy explanation behind the superstition of knocking on wood, but there is another story."}, {"time": "14500", "image": "engenn8le17ob05re2img01.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "This story involves me five years ago at my aunt and uncle's wedding anniversary. The conversation had turned to cars and eventually to car accidents. My family members all recalled being in car accidents and when I mentioned not having an accident, they all exclaimed I better knock on wood. I laughed and refused to knock on anything wooden, despite the warnings of my aunt and uncle because I wasn't superstitious ... yet."}, {"time": "39500", "image": "engenn8le17ob05re2img02.jpg", "id": 3, "text": "Anyway, after all of the presents were opened and after the cake was eaten, it was time to go home. I walked down the street to get in my car and drive home, but what I found was shocking. My car had been  destroyed by someone who hit it and then drove off.  The door was smashed. The window was broken and the side mirror was completely torn off. In my country, if you damage another person's car you are supposed to stay and wait. At the very least, you are supposed to leave a note with a phone number. I was a victim of a hit-and-run. <br/>\nSo after that night, I always make sure to knock on wood."}]}}], "id": 1}], "id": 0}], "type": "sena"}